  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ87dRg5V",
      "title": "[codex] fix proxyd interop access-list namespace",
      "author": "karlfloersch",
      "number": 623,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nUpdates proxyd interop access-list validation to call `interop_checkAccessList` directly instead of using the pinned op-geth helper that still calls `supervisor_checkAccessList`.\n\n## Why\n\n`ethereum-optimism/optimism#20778` moved op-interop-filter's query API to the `interop` RPC namespace. Proxyd still depended on op-geth's `InteropClient`, whose `CheckAccessList` method sends the old `supervisor_checkAccessList` method.\n\nI checked the available client libraries before making this local wrapper change: the current OP `op-service/sources.SupervisorClient` and the pinned op-geth helper both still use the legacy namespace, so a small proxyd-side RPC call is the narrowest fix.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test . -run TestPerformCheckAccessListOpUsesInteropNamespace -count=1`\n- `go test ./integration_tests -run TestInteropValidation_NormalFlow -count=1 -timeout=90s`\n\nNote: `go test ./...` reached the existing `proxyd/integration_tests` 10m timeout in a broader run; the focused interop validation flow passes when run directly.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-19T22:13:20Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 54,
      "deletions": 6
    }
